il reliably.  It's a heap-buffer-overflow on `strlen(query)` in `pgss_store`.  Will look into it some more.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/673199197/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/673764824","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/5386#issuecomment-673764824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/5386","id":673764824,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY3Mzc2NDgyNA==","user":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-08-13T23:51:42Z","updated_at":"2020-08-13T23:51:42Z","body":"From `PreCommit_Portals`, `portal->queryDesc->sourceText` is the `query` variable above.  It also happens to be equal to `portal->sourceText`.\r\n\r\nOn my dev server, `portal->sourceText` is `0x62500000b3c0`.  ASAN failure shows\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow on address 0x62500000c100\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe difference is 3392 (decimal).  Doing a `strnlen(portal->sourceText, 3392)` is fine, but doing a `strnlen(portal->sourceText, 3393)` causes the heap overflow.\r\n\r\nAlso, it appears that the `sourceText` is garbage because first character was 0x7f.  I'm guessing that's why the strlen went too far.  Probably either `sourceText` wasn't initialized or it's a bad pointer.  `portal->name` also doesn't have readable text, but `portal->portalContext->name` is `PortalContext`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/673764824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://a