native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-3535](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-3535)\r\n### Description\n\npgwrapper libpq C++ code has a faulty macro EXEC_STATUS_SWITCH_CASE that returns a bad string.  It is exposed commonly by functions PGConn::Execute and PGConn::Fetch.  These functions are mostly used in YSQL C++ tests and for internal tserver-postgres unix domain socket connections, such as index backfill and ysql upgrade.\r\n\r\nThe string shows itself in messages like\r\n\r\n```\r\nW0914 15:14:15.400462 1795894 libpq_utils.cc:83] SQLSTATE is not defined for result with error message: server closed the connection unexpectedly\r\n        This probably means the server terminated abnormally\r\n        before or while processing the request.\r\n, PQresultStatus: BOOST_PP_SEQ_HEAD((PGRES_FATAL_ERROR) (PGRES_COPY_BOTH) (PGRES_SINGLE_TUPLE))\r\n```\r\n\r\nSee the \"BOOST_PP_SEQ_HEAD\" in the message.\r\n\r\nThe issue has been around for a while, at least 2 years back according to issue comment https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/5386#issuecomment-674577161.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14040/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14040/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]